   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing South-South and triangular industrial cooperation through UNIDO Centre for South-South Industrial Cooperation China (Phase 4)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UNIDO Centre for South-South Industrial Cooperation (UCSSIC China), established in 2008 following agreements between UNIDO and China, aims to enhance industrial cooperation between China and other developing countries. Having completed three previous phases focused on strengthening partnerships, promoting green industrial parks, sharing knowledge, and facilitating technology transfer, the Centre is now entering its fourth phase. This new phase will continue to operationalize South-South and Triangular Industrial Cooperation (SSTIC) - a key cross-cutting priority for UNIDO, which has a long-standing successful partnership with China - to advance UNIDO&apos;s &quot;Progress by Innovation&quot; mandate through strengthened coordination with various partners and programs.</narrative>
  </description>
